# Live counter data — pick ONE of the two sources below.
#
# Option A (preferred): Apps Script web app. More reliable and avoids CORS/CSV quirks.
#   1. Open https://script.google.com and create a new project.
#   2. Paste the contents of apps-script/Code.gs into the editor.
#   3. Create a Google Sheet (any name) and note its ID from the URL.
#   4. In Apps Script: set SHEET_ID = '...' and SHEET_NAME = 'Sheet1' near the top of Code.gs.
#   5. Deploy -> New deployment -> Type: Web app -> Execute as: Me -> Who has access: Anyone -> Deploy.
#   6. Copy the /exec URL and paste it below.
#   7. In FormSubmit dashboard, link the RSVP form to the same Google Sheet so submissions become rows.
#   8. Counter in Vercel goes live -> numbers update every 30s.
# Format: https://script.google.com/macros/s/<id>/exec
NEXT_PUBLIC_RSVP_COUNTER_URL=
#
# Option B (fallback): Published-as-CSV URL of the Google Sheet that FormSubmit writes to.
#   1. In FormSubmit dashboard, link your RSVP form to a Google Sheet.
#   2. Open the Sheet -> File -> Share -> Publish to web -> select your sheet ->
#      choose "Comma-separated values (.csv)" and copy the URL.
#   3. Paste the URL below (looks like https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<id>/pub?gid=0&single=true&output=csv).
# Leave both empty to keep the Counter visible but in "Setup needed" state with zeros.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RSVP_SHEET_CSV=